    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33611" root="فرطح" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَأْسٌ مُفَرْطَحٌ</span></b>  <i>A broad,</i> or <i>wide, head;</i> (S, K;)
as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِرْطَاحٌ</span></b> : the former is thus accord. to J;
but it is [said to be] correctly <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُفَلْطَحٌ</span>, with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ل</span>:
(K:) [or] both are correct; <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ر</span> being a letter which
replaces <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ل</span>. (MF.)

